    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0062" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/163<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >5/8</hi>a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-04T15:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1940—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>239. Department’s circular telegram July 11, 4 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d56-f1"
                    /> The proposed staff conversations between representatives of the United States
                    Army and Navy and of the armies and navies of the other American republics are
                    scheduled to take place at various times beginning around August 19. Lieutenant
                    Colonel L. W. Miller, U. S. Army, and Captain A. T. Beauregard, U. S. Navy, have
                    been designated respectively to represent the War and Navy Departments in the
                    proposed staff conversations with Brazilian officials. You are authorized to
                    inform them that they may begin their conversations at any time which is
                    agreeable to the Brazilian authorities.</p>
                <pb facs="0063" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>
                <p>A separate telegram<anchor n="66" xml:id="d56-f2"/> is being sent you outlining
                    the agenda for the proposed conversations, which you may communicate in
                    strictest confidence to the appropriate Brazilian authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
